// <auto-generated>ANG doc 96: the server's combat events played on the humanoid bodies. Presentation only.</auto-generated>
// Go has already resolved every AP, hit, wound, stun and position when an event reaches Unity. This file plays the
// published events in their order as beats: a step walks the cells the server moved the body through, a blow plays
// the clip of the weapon seen in hand (its mode told apart by the event's AP and the CUE look), the target reacts at
// the clip's impact share (hit / parry / knocked out — whatever the event and the current state say), a dressing
// kneels. Clips, props and timing come from CUE (world.combat_look via the playable scene presentation). A state the
// cast does not have falls back to its idle and is logged once. Nothing here sends a command or decides an outcome.
